<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Bagration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Belorussian strategic offensive · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Bagration was the Soviet summer offensive of 1944 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, launched on 22–23 June. It destroyed most of the German Army Group Centre, one of the greatest defeats in German military history, and carried the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> and the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a> by August. It began about two weeks after the Allied landings in Normandy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-bagration.jpg" alt="Operation Bagration" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Army · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BagrationMap2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
